    "result_text": "The full build compiles cleanly (validating the generated `OwnerDto` and the MapStruct mapper) and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `customerCode`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `checkDigit` field (integer, 0\u20139) to the owner schema, right after `customerCode`. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `checkDigit` property at build time.\n\n2. **`util/LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 A pure-function utility computing the standard Luhn check digit over the decimal digits in a string, mirroring the style of the existing `LocalityResolver`.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` that populates `checkDigit` via `LuhnCheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`, alongside the other derived fields.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`, which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit, passes \u2014 and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
